[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     6[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Axis enumeration (from the source, not from guesses)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     7[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     8[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### Axis 1 — entry point (the FULL set of exported entry points)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     9[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    10[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `nm -D --defined-only c_src/build/libdriver.so` exports exactly two:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    11[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    12[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `printHexCharLine(char)` — the **low-level** entry point. It is absent from
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `driver.h` but is non-`static`, so it is dynamically callable and must be
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   exercised directly, not just through its caller.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `driver(char)` — the one-shot **convenience wrapper**; its whole body is
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `char result = data + 1; printHexCharLine(result);`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### Axis 2 — runtime options / modes / flags
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```sh
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m grep -n "if\|switch\|#ifdef\|#if" c_src/src/driver.c c_src/include/driver.h
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Zero hits other than the `#ifndef DRIVER_H_` header guard. There are **no**
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m runtime options, no modes, no flags, no globals, no init/config function, and no
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m conditional compilation. This axis has exactly one level: *(none)*. So the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m cross-product is Axis 1 × Axis 3.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### Axis 3 — input shape the code special-cases
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The parameter is a single by-value `char`, so there is no size, width, count,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m element type, format, byte order, or emptiness axis. The shape axis is the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    33[0m:[38;5;10m[49m *value* axis, and the value sub-ranges the behaviour actually distinguishes are
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    34[0m:[38;5;10m[49m determined by two ABI facts the C code depends on:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    35[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    36[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 1. On the target ABI (x86-64 Linux) `char` is **signed**. Passing it to the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    37[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    variadic `printf` applies the integer promotions, **sign-extending** to `int`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    38[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `%02x` then reinterprets that `int` as `unsigned int`. Therefore the sign bit
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    39[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    of the argument selects between two visibly different output widths:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    40[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    * `0x00..=0x7F` (non-negative) → 2 hex digits, e.g. `41`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    41[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    * `0x80..=0xFF` (negative)     → 8 hex digits, e.g. `ffffff80`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 2. `%02x` has a minimum field width of 2, so values `0x00..=0x0F` are
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    43[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    zero-padded (`00`..`0f`) while `0x10..=0x7F` are not.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    44[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 3. In `driver`, `data + 1` is computed in promoted `int` and truncated back to
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    45[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `char`, so `data == 0x7F` crosses into the negative sub-range and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    46[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `data == 0xFF` wraps to `0x00`. The `+1` therefore **shifts** every boundary
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    47[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    in axis 3 by one relative to `printHexCharLine`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    48[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    49[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Configuration rows
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    50[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    51[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Rows are the pruned cross-product of Axis 1 × Axis 3 — one row per combination
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    52[0m:[38;5;10m[49m the C actually treats differently. Every row is driven with **many randomized
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    53[0m:[38;5;10m[49m inputs** drawn from that row's sub-range using a fixed-seed xorshift PRNG (seed
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    54[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `0x2025_0901_DEADBEEF`), except the exhaustive rows which enumerate their whole
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    55[0m:[38;5;10m[49m domain.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    56[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
