[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      83[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      84[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Symptom.** `printHexCharLine(0x100)` printed `00` from the C `.so` and `100`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      85[0m:[38;5;10m[49m from the Rust `.so`. Caught by the Phase C row
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      86[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `errors_out_of_range_int_passed_as_char_arg`, which passes full-width `int`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      87[0m:[38;5;10m[49m values through the ABI-compatible widened signature `void f(int)`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      88[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      89[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Root cause (read from the machine code, C is ground truth).** GCC compiles
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      90[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `void printHexCharLine(char charHex)` to
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      91[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      92[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```text
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      93[0m:[38;5;10m[49m mov    %edi,%eax
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      94[0m:[38;5;10m[49m mov    %al,-0x4(%rbp)      ; spill only the LOW BYTE  -> truncation
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      95[0m:[38;5;10m[49m movsbl -0x4(%rbp),%eax     ; reload sign-extended     -> promotion
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      96[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      97[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      98[0m:[38;5;10m[49m so the callee **re-narrows** the incoming argument register to 8 bits. The Rust
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      99[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `extern "C" fn(c_char)` compiled to a bare `mov %edi,%esi`, because the SysV
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     100[0m:[38;5;10m[49m AMD64 ABI permits the callee to assume the caller already narrowed. For any
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     101[0m:[38;5;10m[49m caller that leaves non-zero high bytes in `%edi` the two libraries disagreed.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     102[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `driver` was already correct — it compiled to `inc %dil; movsbl %dil,%esi`, which
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     103[0m:[38;5;10m[49m only ever touches the low byte, matching GCC's `mov %al` / `movzbl` pair.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     104[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     105[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Fix (`src/lib.rs`).** Declare both exports as taking `c_int` — ABI-identical to
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     106[0m:[38;5;10m[49m the `char` declaration in `driver.h`, since the argument travels in the same
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     107[0m:[38;5;10m[49m register — and truncate explicitly:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     108[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     109[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```rust
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     110[0m:[38;5;10m[49m let narrowed: c_char = charHex as c_char;   // reproduces `mov %al`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     111[0m:[38;5;10m[49m let promoted:  c_int = narrowed as c_int;   // reproduces `movsbl`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     112[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     113[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     114[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `printHexCharLine` now compiles to `movsbl %dil,%esi`, the exact net effect of
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     115[0m:[38;5;10m[49m GCC's three instructions. Behaviour for a well-behaved caller passing a real
